<title>UK: LME lists primary aluminium, delists alloy brand.</title>
<headline>LME lists primary aluminium, delists alloy brand.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The London Metal Exchange (LME) has approved the listing of the AE aluminium brand produced by Aluminium Essen GMBH at its German plant.</p>
<p>The brand will constitute good delivery against LME contracts with immediate effect.</p>
<p>Another LME notice said that the LME was delisting the Australian aluminium alloy brand AFFINITY produced by Affinity Metals.</p>
<p>No further deliveries will be permitted of this brand after May 13 and once stocks are exhausted the brand will be delisted.</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
</text>
